Patch summary:
A Vulkan app that signals a semaphore exported as a sync fd no longer waits
for the GPU to finish all its work at every submission. With virtio-gpu
native sync and no fence passing, gfxstream's guest makes an exportable
semaphore's sync fd when the semaphore is created, from a host export that
the host does not wait on for semaphores, so the fd is signaled at once; to
keep it honest, vkQueueSubmit waited for the queue to go idle before
returning whenever it signaled such a semaphore. Skia does that every frame,
in SurfaceFlinger's Vulkan RenderEngine and in every app's HWUI, so neither
could record a frame while the GPU drew the last one: under WSL2 at 144 Hz
SurfaceFlinger missed every frame of a window being scrolled. Now the
submission is followed by an empty one that signals a new exportable fence,
the host waits for that fence asynchronously, and the semaphores get its
sync fd. A fence is used once and destroyed after its fd has signaled, as a
reset could reach the host after the export it would race.

